-- BRACES AS A BLOCK -------------------------------------------- main.kl  K0905

Kalam blocks don't use `{ … }`. A block starts with `:` at the end of a line and continues on the lines indented one level deeper.

2│     if n < 0 { return "negative" }
                ^

Try: `: `

Help: Replace `{` with `:` at the end of the line, indent the body by 4 spaces, and delete the closing `}`. `kalam fix` does this for you.

Learn more: kalam explain K0905
